WEBVTT

00:00:29.658 --> 00:00:33.186
and it was an explosion
that was mind-numbing.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.071
If you took every
nuclear weapon ever built

00:00:36.095 --> 00:00:37.654
at the height of the Cold War,

00:00:37.678 --> 00:00:39.050
lumped them together,

00:00:39.074 --> 00:00:41.576
and blew them up at the same time,

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.309
that would be one one-millionth
of the energy released at that moment.

00:00:46.996 --> 00:00:50.486
The dinosaurs had a really bad day.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:51.675
OK?

00:00:51.699 --> 00:00:54.040
Now, a six-mile-wide rock is very large.

00:00:54.064 --> 00:00:55.429
We all live here in Boulder.

00:00:55.453 --> 00:00:57.853
If you look out your window
and see Longs Peak --

00:00:57.877 --> 00:00:59.592
you're probably familiar with it --

00:00:59.616 --> 00:01:02.629
now, scoop up Longs Peak
and put it out in space.